  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_d1a62a89ce3346009688730875c43673",
      "statement": "step ca renew defaults to renewing after two-thirds of a certificate's validity (expires-in = period/3) and computes the next delay as the remaining lifetime minus expires-in with random jitter up to period/20 (fully random when less than period/20 remains); --renew-period fixes the interval but requires --daemon and is mutually exclusive with --expires-in, and both must not exceed the certificate validity period.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://command/ca/renew.go#L262-L321",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a698728cd5f232fa8e7a47525d76d282b5f18cd4873002a36ef5f5d4934056ad:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://command/ca/renew.go#L354-L380",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:01ffbad2ae3f1aae3edb8f558cef5e6ddc34ca88f58078614ce4581c2896bcf8:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_43e46e6dc79142d08c756f4b25d3438c",
      "statement": "In non-daemon mode --expires-in acts as a skip gate: renewal exits successfully without acting when the remaining lifetime exceeds expires-in plus random jitter of expires-in/20.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://command/ca/renew.go#L340-L347",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:7adf1411562a86078f1963770378333eb56d61e7eb3104a6f321a8233d5fe39c:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_0ce8242035524418ac6b5e50fd7ac18f",
      "statement": "The daemon loop treats SIGINT/SIGTERM as graceful exits and SIGHUP as force-renew-now, retries failed renewals after a fixed one-minute durationOnErrors, and always forces --force so output files are overwritten.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://command/ca/renew.go#L370-L374",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:1efc77ab627bdef4146d5c828e8cfcf0d1a1bdf1e2906272d8254f07b8750f83:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://command/ca/renew.go#L549-L556",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:2a6617e75b11d272695c568be7d07233b51c94326875946b5adf0ca8af187f35:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://command/ca/renew.go#L586-L618",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5c04f90b70056121236c64ab6d05ce427d04ca902a9a36d30dc6130060203c2a:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_c0a03b62fd5e4f7bae0973db624b966d",
      "statement": "After each successful daemon renewal, the written chain is re-read from disk, the new leaf and key are swapped into the live TLS transport, and the next delay is recomputed from the renewed certificate.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://command/ca/renew.go#L549-L583",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:2c325e55419ba3d2978d9b9f92c6c28f19e3cce0bab331f251837884cf29c1a2:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_5f4ac2df52ad480f81796a1a70df7025",
      "statement": "Post-renewal hooks run after every successful renewal: runKillPid sends --signal (default SIGHUP) to --pid or the PID read from --pid-file (mutually exclusive, positive values required), then runExecCmd executes the --exec string as a whitespace-split child with step's stdio.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://command/ca/renew.go#L382-L408",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4024fd2183de8e66041b95d92e6932bbc7b60e1b9091eac1bd62ed29632c3acc:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_f38ea02970d3406a8e26787ddfa757c3",
      "statement": "Renewal authenticates over an mTLS transport (TLS >= 1.2, proxy from environment, client certificate attached only while the current leaf is valid) by default via the BoolT --mtls flag, and with --mtls=false mints an x5c-insecure renewal token from the cert/key and calls RenewWithToken; offline mode swaps the online client for an OfflineCA.",
      "evidence": [
